<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Holy Synod</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1721">1721</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Holy Synod was the governing body of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-orthodox-church">Russian Orthodox Church</a> established by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-the-great">Peter the Great</a> in 1721, replacing the office of patriarch. It was overseen by a lay official appointed by the tsar. It placed the church under state control, a key part of Peter's reforms in the foundation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/holy-synod.jpg" alt="Holy Synod" width="320" height="199" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: anonimus · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Highest_authority_of_Russian_Orthodox_Church_in_1917.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
